course: dictionary
lesson: 12659
title: Dissemination: spreading something widely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dissemination is a long, formal word. It means spreading something so that many people, or many places, get it. Look for the clues around it. «The newspaper led the dissemination of the news to thousands of readers.» Newspapers reach thousands of people, so dissemination must mean sharing the news widely.
explain: Dissemination often goes with words like information, knowledge and ideas. «The dissemination of knowledge helps everyone learn.» Knowledge is what we know, so dissemination here means spreading it so more people can learn. Swap in the word spreading and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In science, dissemination means spreading seeds, disease or something through an area. «Wind carries dandelion seeds across the field, which is one way of dissemination.» Scientists also call this dispersal. Notice that the meaning changes with the subject, so the clues around the word matter.
fact: Dissemination means spreading something widely, so that many people or places get it.
fact: Dissemination is a formal word, often used in news, research and school subjects.
fact: Common phrases are «the dissemination of information» and «the dissemination of knowledge».
fact: In science, dissemination is the spreading of seeds, disease or something through an area; it is also called dispersal.
fact: «The dissemination of false information» means spreading untrue facts, which is what fake news does.
exercise: «The charity worked on the dissemination of safety advice to every home in the town.» What does dissemination mean here? | Writing the advice in a very old book | Locking the advice away in a safe | *Spreading the advice widely so many people get it | Cutting the advice into short pieces
exercise: «Wind carries dandelion seeds across the field, which is one way of dissemination.» In science, what does dissemination mean? | Burning dry leaves in autumn | *Spreading seeds through an area | Counting the seeds in a packet | Growing one seed in a pot
exercise: Maya says dissemination means a heavy shower of rain. What does it really mean? | *Spreading information or ideas widely | A heavy shower of rain | A kind of slow dance | A small hidden room
test: «The school used a newsletter for the dissemination of news about the trip.» What does dissemination mean? | Forgetting the news quickly | Keeping the news secret in a drawer | *Sharing the news widely with everyone | Writing the news in a diary
test: Another name for the science meaning of dissemination, the spreading of seeds, is which word? | dismissal | desert | disguise | *dispersal
exam: «Fake news spreads because of the dissemination of false information online.» What does the dissemination of false information mean? | Keeping information private | Checking facts before sharing them | *Spreading untrue information widely | Writing a true report for a class
